  "id": "attenuated-positive-symptoms",
  "term": "attenuated positive symptoms",
  "definition": "Attenuated positive symptoms are milder, residual forms of positive psychotic symptoms that can remain after a schizophrenia episode, rather than full delusions, hallucinations, or disorganized speech or behavior. In the packet, odd beliefs are given as an example.",
