      "reasons": [
        "The packet describes a subtype of schizophrenia (residual type schizophrenia), not the standalone term sense given in the definition.",
        "The claim that attenuated positive symptoms are generally \"milder, residual forms of positive psychotic symptoms\" is not directly supported by the packet; the packet only says residual symptoms may include attenuated positive symptoms such as odd beliefs.",
        "The definition adds interpretive wording about what these symptoms are \"rather than\" full delusions, hallucinations, or disorganized speech or behavior; the packet instead says those features are absent in residual type schizophrenia, not that this is the definition of attenuated positive symptoms."
